WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.391
Use the decoder after learning the families.

2
00:00:03.391 --> 00:00:09.481
CVE2 is a family and repository label; CV32E20 adds width and product identity.

3
00:00:09.481 --> 00:00:17.574
CV32E40 siblings share a 32-bit embedded four-stage prefix, while P, X, and S route to different manuals.

4
00:00:17.574 --> 00:00:23.894
CVA6 names the configurable repository; CV64A60 is its formal part-number example.

5
00:00:23.894 --> 00:00:31.294
CV32A60AX comes from the configuration table, while the current index separately links CV32A65X.

6
00:00:31.294 --> 00:00:37.075
Resolve the remaining identifier through the matching document and release.

